 "about": "The NFL hub's ELO Model on NBA box scores: every player an Elo rating moved after each final by his Game Score plus on-court plus-minus against a regular's typical game and the opposing club's unit, each club's expected rotation of eight weighted by rating, and the home win chance a logistic on the home-minus-away strengths and home court and back to backs, with no intercept. The spread is the same logit times a fitted slope. Who plays: every call in games (a final, a game under way, a game of today or to come) on the club's previous box-scored game's rotation, less anyone who has since played for another club (a club's first game of a season on its last game of the season before), never this run's roster or report or the injury log; upcoming, the games not yet final, on the hub's injury rule and today's roster and report. Fitted on finished seasons only, never refitted by the job. The Elo picks price its legs pulled toward the market (params.pick).",
